    #      recursive removal written as a command (the command word followed by
    #      a quoted or expanded target) is classified: RULED when every target
    #      is a quoted ${NAME:?} expansion, alone or followed by a path inside
    #      the quotes; STANDING when it sits outside the log's printed-script
    #      blocks (a block from a heading "## script..." to the next "## "
    #      heading) and its line, leading space dropped, is a line of a
    #      committed script under scripts/ at the phase commit, which is how the
    #      logs print the sourced counting library; UNRULED otherwise. Every
    #      count of unruled must be 0; this script's own source admits no
    #      standing line. A mention in prose (the command word not followed by a
    #      target) is not a command and is not counted. Controls through the
    #      same function over fixtures built from pieces: an unruled target in a
    #      script block counts 1; ruled single and path targets count 0
    #      unruled; the library's own line outside a script block is standing;
    #      the same line inside a script block is unruled; a command naming one
    #      ruled and one unruled target counts 1. This script's own trap now
    #      writes its target in the ruled form.
